# Line endings are part of the build here, not a preference.
#
# `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` runs in CI and reads .editorconfig, so git and
# .editorconfig must agree about end_of_line on EVERY platform. Without this file they do
# not: a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF working files, a Linux CI
# checkout of the same commit produces LF, and whichever one disagrees with .editorconfig
# fails the format step with ENDOFLINE on every line of every file.
#
# LF is the normalised form: it is what the index already stores, so pinning it here changes
# no committed bytes - and the bash `run:` blocks in .github/workflows stay LF, where a CR
# would reach the shell as part of the command.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary content must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pfx binary
*.snk binary

# Generated lock files: kept in the repo on purpose, never hand-edited.
packages.lock.json -diff
